#: ../../../dev/crashrep.rst:60
msgid "Wire Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/crashrep.rst:62
msgid "To upload a crash report we need three things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/crashrep.rst:64
msgid "The data comprising the report as above,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/crashrep.rst:65
msgid "the SHA-256 hash of the report data, making up the report ID, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/crashrep.rst:66
msgid "the base URL to send the report to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/crashrep.rst:68
msgid ""
"The report URL is constructed by adding the report ID to the base URL. The "
"default base URL of ``https://crash.syncthing.net/newcrash/`` and the report "
"ID ``abcd1234`` results in the URL ``https://crash.syncthing.net/newcrash/"
"abcd1234``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/crashrep.rst:73
msgid ""
"First a ``HEAD`` request is performed on the report URL. If this request "
"returns successfully (``200 OK``) it means the server already has the report "
"ID in question. We do not need to upload it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/crashrep.rst:77
msgid ""
"If the HEAD request returns ``404 Not Found`` or another error we can "
"attempt to upload the report. This is done by a ``PUT`` request to the same "
"URL with the report data as the body."
msgstr ""
